---
const title = 'Media & Field Notes | USIVA Planning Artifacts';
const description = 'Inspect USIVA visual aids for readiness files, pathway sequencing, authorization boundaries, and source trails.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/media-gallery.html';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://usiva.org/assets/usiva-social.svg" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="USIVA — visa-readiness and compliance planning" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#e2eeea" />
  </head>
  <body class="gallery-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header"><div class="gallery-wrap header-inner"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="USIVA home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">US</span><span><strong>USIVA</strong><small>Media / field notes / visual aids</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/services.html">Services</a><a href="/about.html">About</a><a href="/pricing.html">Scope &amp; fees</a><a href="/blog.html">Field notes</a><a class="nav-cta" href="/contacts.html">Start a question</a></nav></div></header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="gallery-hero"><div class="gallery-wrap gallery-hero__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Media / planning artifacts</p><h1>A gallery for the work before approval.</h1><p class="hero-lede">USIVA uses simple visual aids to make a readiness file, pathway sequence, authorization boundary, or source trail easier to inspect. These are original HTML and CSS diagrams — not government forms, client stories, metrics, or proof of an outcome.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button--ink" href="#gallery">Enter the gallery</a><a class="under-link" href="/services.html">Use the planning map →</a></div></div><aside class="gallery-note"><span>Exhibition note</span><strong>Look for the question each artifact makes easier to ask.</strong><p>Every diagram has a text caption and a plain-language limitation.</p></aside></div></section>

      <section class="gallery-intro" aria-labelledby="intro-heading"><div class="gallery-wrap gallery-intro__grid"><p class="folio">FIELD STUDY<br /><span>01</span></p><div><p class="eyebrow">Why visual aids</p><h2 id="intro-heading">A picture can organize a conversation without pretending to decide it.</h2><p>There is no public case-study media archive on this site. The gallery is a small set of reusable planning metaphors: a file you can sort, a path you can sequence, a boundary you can name, and a source trail you can revisit.</p><p>Use the captions. They describe the role and the limit of each artifact.</p></div></div></section>

      <section class="gallery-wall" id="gallery" aria-labelledby="gallery-heading"><div class="gallery-wrap"><div class="wall-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The wall</p><h2 id="gallery-heading">Four ways to see the next question.</h2></div><div class="wall-grid">
        <figure class="artifact-card artifact-card--file"><div class="artifact artifact-file" role="img" aria-label="A planning file with identity, academic, and funding sections"><div class="file-tab">READINESS FILE</div><div class="file-title">Before the deadline</div><div class="file-rule file-rule--long"></div><div class="file-rule file-rule--short"></div><div class="file-sections"><span>IDENTITY</span><span>ACADEMIC</span><span>FUNDING</span></div><div class="file-rule file-rule--medium"></div><div class="file-stamp">CHECK / DATE / ASK</div></div><figcaption><strong>01 / The readiness file</strong><span>Sort records by the decision they support. This drawing does not define a required document list; the relevant school, sponsor, or authority does.</span></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="artifact-card artifact-card--path"><div class="artifact artifact-path" role="img" aria-label="A three-step pathway from prepare to verify to hand off"><div class="path-label">PATHWAY / NOT A GUARANTEE</div><div class="path-line"><span>PREPARE</span><i></i><span>VERIFY</span><i></i><span>HAND OFF</span></div><div class="path-foot"><b>file</b><b>source</b><b>owner</b></div></div><figcaption><strong>02 / The pathway map</strong><span>Sequence the next handoff instead of jumping to an outcome. The sequence changes when the program, status, location, or facts change.</span></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="artifact-card artifact-card--boundary"><div class="artifact artifact-boundary" role="img" aria-label="Three lanes labeled study, research, and work meeting an ask first marker"><div class="boundary-caption">ACTIVITY / ASK FIRST</div><div class="lane-line"><span>STUDY</span><b></b></div><div class="lane-line"><span>RESEARCH</span><b></b></div><div class="lane-line"><span>WORK</span><b></b></div><strong class="ask-marker">ASK<br />FIRST</strong></div><figcaption><strong>03 / The authorization boundary</strong><span>Separate activities before assuming they share a permission. This is a visual prompt, not a determination that any activity is authorized.</span></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="artifact-card artifact-card--source"><div class="artifact artifact-source" role="img" aria-label="A source trail connecting a public source to local instructions and a specialist question"><div class="source-top">SOURCE TRAIL</div><div class="source-stack"><span>PUBLIC SOURCE</span><i></i><span>LOCAL INSTRUCTION</span><i></i><span>SPECIALIST QUESTION</span></div><div class="source-foot">CHECKED / DATE / FIT</div></div><figcaption><strong>04 / The source trail</strong><span>Keep the source, date, and fit visible. A public page may orient you while a school, sponsor, agency, or attorney controls the answer.</span></figcaption></figure>
      </div></div></section>

      <section class="gallery-reading" aria-labelledby="reading-heading"><div class="gallery-wrap gallery-reading__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">How to use the wall</p><h2 id="reading-heading">Notice what the artifacts refuse to claim.</h2></div><div class="reading-list"><p><span class="reading-number">01</span><span class="reading-copy"><strong>No invented evidence.</strong> There are no client logos, outcomes, testimonials, or pseudo-metrics here.</span></p><p><span class="reading-number">02</span><span class="reading-copy"><strong>No substitute for a source.</strong> The drawings organize questions; they do not replace current official or program instructions.</span></p><p><span class="reading-number">03</span><span class="reading-copy"><strong>No shortcut around a handoff.</strong> When facts become personal, the next step is a responsible authority or licensed counsel.</span></p></div></div></section>

      <section class="gallery-next" aria-labelledby="next-heading"><div class="gallery-wrap gallery-next__inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">Take the artifact with you</p><h2 id="next-heading">Turn a visual prompt into a verified question.</h2><p>Choose the planning page that matches the artifact you need: file, route, boundary, or source.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button button--red" href="/services.html">Open services</a><a class="button button--quiet" href="/tips-faq.html">Read the FAQ</a></div></div></section>

      <section class="notice"><div class="gallery-wrap"><strong>Important notice:</strong> These visual aids are informational planning content. They are not official government documents, legal advice, or a guarantee of admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, or government approval.</div></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer"><div class="gallery-wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="footer-brand" href="/">USIVA</a><p>Visa-readiness and compliance planning for international study and research pathways.</p></div><div><p class="footer-label">Explore</p><a href="/services.html">Services</a><a href="/about.html">About USIVA</a><a href="/pricing.html">Scope &amp; fees</a></div><div><p class="footer-label">Read</p><a href="/blog.html">Field notes</a><a href="/tips-faq.html">Tips &amp; FAQ</a><a href="/contacts.html">Start a question</a></div><div><p class="footer-label">External path</p><a href="https://usfellows.org/international-rd-scholars.html">US Fellows International R&amp;D Scholars ↗</a><p>Visual aids are not a substitute for the authority responsible for your situation.</p></div></div><div class="gallery-wrap footer-bottom">© 2026 USIVA · A US Council companion site.</div></footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; background: #fbfaf7; color: #172231; font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; line-height: 1.65; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
  :global(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  :global(a:focus-visible) { outline: 3px solid #d0a85c; outline-offset: 4px; }
  :global(p) { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: #5c6974; }
  :global(h1), :global(h2), :global(h3) { margin: 0 0 .7rem; color: #0a253f; font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.08; }
  :global(h1) { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7.2vw, 7rem); letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  :global(h2) { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.2vw, 4.3rem); letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .gallery-wrap { width: min(1160px, calc(100% - 48px)); margin-inline: auto; }
  .skip-link { position: fixed; top: -4rem; left: 1rem; z-index: 20; padding: .7rem 1rem; background: #fff; color: #0a253f; font-weight: 800; }
  .skip-link:focus { top: 1rem; }
  .site-header { background: #fbfaf7; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8dfe1; }
  .header-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; min-height: 5.6rem; }
  .brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; }
  .brand-mark { display: grid; width: 2.8rem; height: 2.8rem; place-items: center; border: 1px solid #b9893e; border-radius: 50%; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .8rem Georgia, serif; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px #fbfaf7, inset 0 0 0 5px #b9893e; }
  .brand strong { display: block; color: #0a253f; font: 700 1.5rem/1 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .brand small { display: block; color: #52616a; font-size: .58rem; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-end; gap: .3rem 1.25rem; color: #334350; font-size: .84rem; font-weight: 750; }
  nav a:hover { color: #ae403a; }
  .nav-cta { padding: .55rem .8rem; border: 1px solid #ae403a; color: #ae403a; }
  .gallery-hero { background: #e2eeea; border-bottom: 1px solid #c8dad5; }
  .gallery-hero__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(18rem, .8fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 8rem); align-items: end; min-height: 39rem; padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  .gallery-hero__grid > div:first-child { max-width: 58rem; }
  .eyebrow, .folio, .footer-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: #ae403a; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .eyebrow--light { color: #efd69b; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 48rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: #40515b; font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.5; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 3rem; padding: .75rem 1.05rem; border: 1px solid #0a253f; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .button--ink { background: #0a253f; color: #fff; }
  .button--red { background: #ae403a; border-color: #ae403a; color: #fff; }
  .button--quiet { border-color: #6c7b83; color: #263844; }
  .button:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .under-link { color: #ae403a; font-size: .87rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .gallery-note { padding: 1.8rem; border: 1px solid #c3d2ce; border-top: 5px solid #0b5f5a; background: #fffdf9; box-shadow: 1rem 1rem 0 rgba(10,37,63,.1); }
  .gallery-note span { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: #ae403a; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .gallery-note strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: #0a253f; font: 600 clamp(1.55rem, 2.7vw, 2.4rem)/1.08 Georgia, serif; }
  .gallery-note p { margin: 0; font-size: .9rem; }
  .gallery-intro { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem); }
  .gallery-intro__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, .3fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 9rem); }
  .folio { margin: .4rem 0 0; color: #ae403a; font: 700 .7rem/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .folio span { display: inline-block; margin-top: .4rem; color: #0a253f; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .gallery-intro__grid > div { max-width: 50rem; }
  .gallery-intro__grid > div p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 1.07rem; }
  .gallery-wall { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem); background: #f2ede4; border-block: 1px solid #e0d9cd; }
  .wall-heading { max-width: 48rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .wall-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .artifact-card { margin: 0; padding: 1rem; background: #fffdf9; border: 1px solid #d5d7d2; }
  .artifact-card--path { background: #e7f0ed; }
  .artifact-card--boundary { background: #e3edf3; }
  .artifact-card--source { background: #f4dfdc; }
  .artifact { position: relative; min-height: 20rem; overflow: hidden; }
  .artifact-file { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; gap: .8rem; padding: 2rem; background: #f7f1e5; border: 1px solid #c8b990; }
  .file-tab { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 2rem; padding: .45rem .7rem; background: #ae403a; color: #fff; font: 700 .65rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .file-title { max-width: 17rem; color: #0a253f; font: 600 clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 3.4rem)/.95 Georgia, serif; }
  .file-rule { height: .5rem; background: #c49a4f; }
  .file-rule--long { width: 80%; }
  .file-rule--short { width: 45%; background: #9fbab4; }
  .file-rule--medium { width: 60%; background: #ae403a; }
  .file-sections { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .file-sections span { padding: .45rem .55rem; border: 1px solid #a8b7b4; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .62rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .file-stamp { margin-top: .4rem; color: #ae403a; font: 700 .65rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; }
  .artifact-path { display: grid; align-content: center; gap: 2rem; padding: 2rem; background: #d7e8e3; border: 1px solid #8cb7ac; }
  .path-label, .source-top, .source-foot, .boundary-caption { color: #0b5f5a; font: 700 .68rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .13em; }
  .path-line { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: .55rem; align-items: center; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .72rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .path-line i { display: block; width: 2rem; height: 1px; background: #ae403a; }
  .path-line i::after { content: "›"; position: relative; left: 1.8rem; top: -.65rem; color: #ae403a; font: 1.2rem Inter, sans-serif; }
  .path-foot { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #8cb7ac; color: #44645f; font-size: .76rem; }
  .artifact-boundary { display: grid; align-content: center; gap: 1.3rem; padding: 2rem; background: #e6f0f4; border: 1px solid #9ab6c8; }
  .boundary-caption { color: #ae403a; }
  .lane-line { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .75rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .lane-line b { display: block; height: .65rem; border-top: 1px solid #6e97ad; border-bottom: 1px solid #6e97ad; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #c49a4f 0 40%, transparent 40% 100%); }
  .ask-marker { position: absolute; right: 1.4rem; bottom: 1.2rem; display: grid; width: 5rem; height: 5rem; place-content: center; border: 2px solid #ae403a; border-radius: 50%; background: #f4dfdc; color: #ae403a; text-align: center; font: 700 .68rem/.95 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; transform: rotate(8deg); }
  .artifact-source { display: grid; align-content: center; gap: 1.6rem; padding: 2rem; background: #f6e5df; border: 1px solid #c98d83; }
  .source-top, .source-foot { color: #ae403a; }
  .source-stack { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: .6rem; }
  .source-stack span { padding: .7rem .8rem; border: 1px solid #ae403a; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .7rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .source-stack span:nth-child(3) { margin-left: 1.6rem; background: #fffdf9; }
  .source-stack span:nth-child(5) { margin-left: 3.2rem; background: #c49a4f; }
  .source-stack i { width: 1px; height: 1rem; margin-left: 1.4rem; border-left: 1px dashed #ae403a; }
  .artifact-card figcaption { display: grid; gap: .35rem; padding: 1rem .25rem .2rem; }
  .artifact-card figcaption strong { color: #0a253f; font: 600 1.25rem Georgia, serif; }
  .artifact-card figcaption span { color: #5c6974; font-size: .87rem; }
  .artifact-card--source figcaption span { color: #4d5962; }
  .gallery-reading { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); background: #071827; }
  .gallery-reading__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 4rem; }
  .gallery-reading h2 { color: #fff; }
  .reading-list { border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); }
  .reading-list p { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 1fr; column-gap: 1rem; padding: 1.1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); color: #d2dfe4; }
  .reading-list .reading-number { color: #f0d798; font: 700 .75rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .reading-list .reading-copy { color: #d2dfe4; }
  .reading-list strong { color: #fff; }
  .gallery-next { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  .gallery-next__inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 2rem; align-items: end; }
  .gallery-next__inner > div:first-child { max-width: 45rem; }
  .gallery-next .actions { margin-top: 0; }
  .notice { padding-block: 1.2rem; background: #f8e7be; color: #36280e; font-size: .88rem; }
  .site-footer { padding-block: 4rem 1.5rem; background: #0b2238; color: #cad7df; }
  .footer-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .7fr .8fr 1.1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  .footer-brand { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: .8rem; color: #fff; font: 700 1.55rem Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .site-footer p { color: #b5c5cf; font-size: .86rem; }
  .site-footer a { display: block; margin: .35rem 0; color: #d9e4e9; font-size: .86rem; }
  .site-footer a:hover { color: #f0d798; }
  .footer-label { margin-bottom: .7rem; color: #efd69b; }
  .footer-bottom { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16); color: #8ea3b0; font-size: .78rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .header-inner { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; padding-block: 1rem; }
    nav { justify-content: flex-start; }
    .gallery-hero__grid, .gallery-intro__grid, .gallery-reading__grid, .gallery-next__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .gallery-hero__grid { min-height: auto; }
    .gallery-note { max-width: 34rem; }
    .gallery-next .actions { margin-top: 1rem; }
    .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .gallery-wrap { width: min(100% - 2rem, 1160px); }
    .gallery-intro__grid { gap: 1.5rem; }
    .wall-grid, .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .artifact { min-height: 16rem; }
    .artifact-file, .artifact-path, .artifact-boundary, .artifact-source { padding: 1.4rem; }
    .path-line { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .35rem; }
    .path-line i { width: 1px; height: 1rem; margin-left: .5rem; }
    .path-line i::after { left: -.25rem; top: .55rem; }
    .lane-line { grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr; }
    .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .actions .button { width: 100%; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { :global(html) { scroll-behavior: auto; } .button:hover { transform: none; } }
</style>
